 site of the 1967 Karisoke Research Center","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC/RDB","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A gorilla-lodge honeymoon (Singita / One&Only / Bisate)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,500-5,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the Virungas'' apex lodges — Singita Kwitonda''s volcano-view suites, One&Only Gorilla''s Nest, Bisate''s cone-shaped villas — fireside luxury after the trek; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"the Virungas'' apex lodges — Singita Kwitonda''s volcano-view suites, One&Only Gorilla''s Nest, Bisate''s cone-shaped villas — fireside luxury after the trek; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Virunga honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Volcanoes?","a":"The trek itself, and the altitude. The gorilla trek is a strenuous, high-altitude (~2,500-3,700m), often muddy rainforest hike — come with moderate fitness; malaria is year-round (prophylaxis + DEET), and it is remote — carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. **FCDO travel advice for Rwanda:** the FCDO advises against all but essential travel to NAMED AREAS — parts of Rusizi District within 10km of the DRC border. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda — page updated 2026-06-10. Quoted unchanged; TravelWell does not state whether this destination lies inside a named area.*","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is the gorilla permit and how do I book it?","a":"US$1,500 per trekker, and with only 98 permits/day it sells out - book 3-6 months ahead through a licensed operator or the Rwanda Development Board (Irembo). Minimum age 15.","source":"volcanoesnationalpark.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How hard is the gorilla trek and what are the rules?","a":"Moderate-to-strenuous: 1-7 hours through steep, muddy, high-altitude forest to reach the family, then max 1 hour with them, 7 m minimum distance, a face mask, max 8 per group, an armed ranger, and no trekking if you''re ill. Porters are available and recommended.","source":"visitrwandagorilla.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Rwanda or Uganda for gorillas in 2026?","a":"Rwanda''s permit is pricier ($1,500 vs Uganda''s $800), and Volcanoes is 2 hours from Kigali. **FCDO travel advice:** for Rwanda the FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named areas (parts of Rusizi District within 10km of the DRC border) — *gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda, updated 2026-06-10*. For Uganda the FCDO names no advisory against travel — *gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda, updated 2026-07-27*. ⛔ Read both before choosing; TravelWell states no preference on safety grounds.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit, and what else can I do?","a":"Best in the drier Jun-Sep and Dec-Feb; beyond the gorillas, track golden monkeys, hike Bisoke''s crater lake, climb Karisimbi, and make the Dian Fossey grave pilgrimage - a 2-3-day stay rewards.","source":"volcanoesparkrwanda.org","si_tag":"globaladv"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Volcanoes NP Rwanda Gorilla Trekking Guide: Permits, Fitness, Best Time & Safety","meta_description":"Plan a Volcanoes National Park gorilla trek - Rwanda''s flagship mountain-gorilla experience in the Virungas: the $1,500 permit and how to book it, the fitness and rules, Dian Fossey''s Karisoke, golden monkeys and volcano hikes, 2 hours from Kigali - with the FCDO advisory, altitude and health intel.","slug":"volcanoes-np-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Volcanoes National Park gorilla trekking","long_tail":["Rwanda gorilla permit cost 2026","gorilla trekking fitness Rwanda","Dian Fossey grave hike","golden monkey trekking Rwanda","Mount Bisoke hike","Rwanda vs Uganda gorillas","is Rwanda safe"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Parc National des Volcans","ingagi","Karisoke","Bisoke","Karisimbi","Kwita Izina","inguge z''izahabu"],"hreflang":["en","fr"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:58Z","source_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-ebola-alert"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"was). Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - the mountain-gorilla trek is primary safari; golden monkeys + volcano hikes + Fossey grave hike = globaladv; Fossey/Karisoke conservation legacy = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"mountain gorilla trekking"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"golden monkeys + Bisoke/Karisimbi volcano hikes + Dian Fossey grave hike"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Singita/One&Only/Bisate/Sabyinyo"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Dian Fossey / Karisoke"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Singita Kwitonda / One&Only Gorilla''s Nest - the Virungas'' apex stays","why_ultra":"volcano-view suites, private guiding + butlered luxury at the forest edge, the gorilla trek from the doorstep","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$2,500-5,000+/night"},{"name":"A private double-gorilla-permit + golden-monkey + Fossey week","why_ultra":"two gorilla treks (different families) + golden monkeys + the Fossey grave hike + a Bisoke climb, privately guided from an ultra lodge","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A 3-park Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Akagera + Nyungwe)","why_ultra":"gorillas + Big-Five Akagera + Nyungwe chimps/canopy walk, private-guided - and it unlocks the Nov-May 30% permit discount","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Volcanoes National Park, Rwanda"},"geo":{"lat":-1.4667,"lng":29.5},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["akagera-np-rwanda","nyungwe-forest-rwanda"]}'::jsonb, 2),
  ('akagera-np-rwanda', '05A', 'Akagera National Park', 'Rwanda', 'Rwanda''s Big Five comeback', 'live', 'verified', 'elephant', 'Rwanda — Akagera', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Rwanda''s only Big-Five savanna park + one of conservation''s great turnarounds - African Parks (with the RDB since 2010) reintroduced lions (2015), black rhinos (2017), and southern white rhinos in 2021 (30) and 2025 (70, ''Rhino Rewild'')","~1,100 km2 of plains, hills and lakes (largest protected wetland in central/eastern Africa); Big Five game drives + Lake Ihema boat safari (hippos, crocs, ~550 birds incl. the shoebill) + night drives","Uncrowded (NatGeo Best of the World 2026) and ~2 hours from Kigali - fly in the morning, game-drive by lunch; completes the 3-park Rwanda circuit with Volcanoes (gorillas) + Nyungwe (chimps)","disclose + consent","Fees 2026: $100/adult, $50/child; sleeping in-park halves the fee nights 2-3 and is FREE from night 4 (up to a week) - a real reason to stay; best Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb","Sold via Rwandan safari DMCs 10-15% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; African Parks fees bundle/pass-through; RWF (~1,467/USD); visa on arrival $30; malaria year-round in the lowland east; AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (police) / 912 ambulance / 111 fire; AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Remote (~2h from Kigali) - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kigali","malaria":"present year-round in the lowland east (chloroquine-resistant) - prophylaxis advised; DEET at dawn/dusk","yellow_fever":"required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US)","activity_note":"Dangerous game at close range - stay in the vehicle, follow the guide, never approach rhino. Lake Ihema boat safari: hippo pods + shoreline crocs - remain seated, limbs in the boat. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:58Z","page_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00","source_country":"rwanda","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Within ~10 km of the DRC border","lvl":4,"except":["Volcanoes National Park"],"note":"Unrest. Multiple armed groups, individuals and military forces operate in North and South Kivu; violence may spill into Rwanda without warning. US government employees need special authorisation to travel here. State states Volcanoes National Park is not included in this area."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"RW","summary":"Some areas carry increased risk — the DRC border zone below is Do Not Travel.","source":"Curated baseline — the previous source is retired; pending re-verification against the UK FCDO","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Sep (esp Jul-Aug, dry, wildlife at water) + Dec holiday","shoulder":"Oct-Nov + Mar (softer rates, good game)","green":"Jan-early Feb (fewer vehicles, lower lodge rates) + Apr-May (long rains, lush, cheapest)","booking_lead":"lodges (few, small) 2-5 mo for Jun-Sep; in-park stay-longer fee break (nights 2-3 half, 4+ free) rewards multi-night; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Jan-Feb + Apr-May value; the 3-park Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera) unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount","event_peaks":"Jul-Aug + Christmas/NY; N-Hemisphere summer","fire_date":"Jun-Sep 4-6 mo out; 3-park circuit (with the gorilla discount) by prior Aug-Sep; position as quiet accessible Big-Five vs crowded Serengeti/Mara"},"jewels":[{"name":"A Big-Five game drive (the comeback)","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$400-1,800/pp/day","timing":"Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb; dry best","draw_rank":1,"hook":"lion, black + white rhino, elephant, buffalo and leopard on rewilded plains — one of Africa''s great conservation success stories, with hardly another vehicle","si":"safari","blurb":"lion, black + white rhino, elephant, buffalo and leopard on rewilded plains — one of Africa''s great conservation success stories, with hardly another vehicle","when":"Jun-Sep + Jan-Feb; dry best","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Rhino tracking","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"within the safari","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"both black rhino and southern white rhino — Akagera is now one of the more reliable rhino parks in East Africa, guide-radio-coordinated","si":"safari","blurb":"both black rhino and southern white rhino — Akagera is now one of the more reliable rhino parks in East Africa, guide-radio-coordinated","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"The Lake Ihema boat safari","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$40-50/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"large hippo pods + shoreline Nile crocodiles are the leading on-water hazards — remain seated, keep limbs in the boat","si":"adventure","blurb":"large hippo pods + shoreline Nile crocodiles are the leading on-water hazards — remain seated, keep limbs in the boat","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"DMC/park","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A night drive","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$40-60/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the nocturnal cast — leopard, hyena, bushbaby, genet — on a guided after-dark drive, an experience the day misses","si":"adventure","blurb":"the nocturnal cast — leopard, hyena, bushbaby, genet — on a guided after-dark drive, an experience the day misses","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"DMC/park","wells":["stay","move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The African Parks conservation story","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the rewilding of Akagera — from war-emptied to full Big Five under African Parks + the RDB, with the \"Rhino Rewild\" translocations","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the rewilding of Akagera — from war-emptied to full Big Five under African Parks + the RDB, with the \"Rhino Rewild\" translocations","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"park/DMC","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["deepdive","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Magashi Camp honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$800-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Wilderness''s tented lakeside camp on a game-rich peninsula — private guiding, boat safaris and Big Five from the doorstep","si":"ultra","blurb":"Wilderness''s tented lakeside camp on a game-rich peninsula — private guiding, boat safaris and Big Five from the doorstep","when":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"An Akagera lakeside honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Sep  + Dec holiday","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Akagera?","a":"Dangerous game and the lake, plus the health advisory - not crime. Free-ranging lion, elephant and rhino at close range - stay in the vehicle and follow your guide; on the Lake Ihema boat safari keep seated among the hippo pods and shoreline crocs. Malaria is year-round in the lowland east (prophylaxis + DEET), and it''s remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Akagera a real Big Five park?","a":"Yes - thanks to one of conservation''s great turnarounds. African Parks (managing with the RDB since 2010) brought back lions (2015) and rhinos (2017), and added white rhinos in 2021 and 2025 - restoring the full Big Five to a park that civil war had emptied.","source":"nationalgeographic.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Akagera?","a":"Jun-Sep and Jan-Feb (dry) - the bush thins, wildlife concentrates at water, and roads stay passable. Jan-early Feb is low season (fewer vehicles, lower lodge rates); the green rains bring lush scenery and birding.","source":"safaribookings.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How does Akagera fit a Rwanda trip, and is it worth it?","a":"Very much: Akagera is ~2 hours from Kigali, so it pairs naturally with the gorillas of Volcanoes and the chimps of Nyungwe into a 3-park Rwanda circuit - and staying in the park (nights 2-3 half-price, night 4+ free) rewards a longer stop.","source":"nationalgeographic.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Rwanda?","a":"Visa on arrival $30 (or online via Irembo); passport valid 6 months. Yellow fever is required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US).","source":"thingstodoinrwanda.com","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Akagera Safari Guide: Rwanda''s Big Five Comeback, Lake Ihema Boat Safari, Fees & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan an Akagera safari - Rwanda''s Big-Five savanna comeback under African Parks (lions, black + white rhinos rewilded), a Lake Ihema boat safari for hippos, crocs and the shoebill, uncrowded and 2 hours from Kigali - with real safety, timing, fees and the 3-park Rwanda circuit.","slug":"akagera-np-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Akagera National Park safari","long_tail":["Akagera Big Five Rwanda","Akagera boat safari Lake Ihema","Akagera rhino reintroduction","Akagera park fees 2026","Rwanda safari and gorillas","is Akagera safe","Akagera vs Serengeti"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Akagera","intare","inkura","Ihema","imvubu","African Parks","shoebill"],"hreflang":["en","fr"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:58Z","source_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-ebola-alert"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"was). Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - Big-Five game drives primary; Lake Ihema boat safari + night drives = globaladv; African Parks/Rhino-Rewild conservation = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"Big Five game drives"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"Lake Ihema boat safari + night drives"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Magashi Camp (Wilderness)"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"African Parks / Rhino Rewild conservation"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Magashi Camp (Wilderness) - Akagera''s apex stay","why_ultra":"a tented lakeside camp on a game-rich peninsula, private guiding, boat safaris + the Big Five at the door","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-2,500+/night"},{"name":"A private Big-Five + boat + rhino-conservation day","why_ultra":"exclusive-vehicle Big Five game drive + the Lake Ihema boat safari + a behind-the-scenes African Parks conservation visit, privately guided","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The 3-park luxury Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera)","why_ultra":"gorillas + chimps/canopy walk + the Big-Five savanna, private-guided - and it unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Akagera National Park, Rwanda"},"geo":{"lat":-1.65,"lng":30.7},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["nyungwe-forest-rwanda","volcanoes-national-park-rwanda"]}'::jsonb, 3),
  ('amboseli-kenya', '05A', 'Amboseli National Park', 'Kenya', 'Elephants under Kilimanjaro', 'live', 'verified', 'elephant', 'Kenya — Amboseli / Kilimanjaro views', '{"safari","ultra","romance","adventure","deepdive","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Elephants under Kilimanjaro - the most iconic backdrop in safari: 1,600+ free-ranging elephants incl. some of the last Super Tuskers; the best Kilimanjaro (5,896m) views are from Amboseli (clearest at dawn Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb, before ~10am cloud)","Four of the Big Five (elephant, lion, buffalo, leopard) - NO rhino (hunted to local extinction 1970s); pair with Laikipia (Ol Pejeta/Lewa) for rhino","The Amboseli Elephant Research Project (founded 1972 by Cynthia Moss) - the longest wild-elephant study on Earth, 3,500+ individuals, matriarchal society; snowmelt swamps + 400+ birds","KWS fee $70/24-hour (proposed $90 under court review); cost ~$400-850/pp/day comfortable-premium, ~$900-2,000 luxury","Sold via Kenya safari DMCs ~10-16%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; KWS fees non-commissionable pass-through; AMREF Flying Doctors for evac","KES (~129/USD) + M-Pesa but safari quoted USD; eTA required; malaria prophylaxis advised (chloroquine-resistant); YF only if arriving from a risk country"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112 / 911 (reliable in cities, weak remote); Kenya Red Cross ambulance 1199; AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Nairobi","malaria":"prophylaxis advised (CDC - Amboseli qualifies, chloroquine-resistant); DEET at dusk","yellow_fever":"compulsory only if arriving from a risk country; CDC recommends for most","activity_note":"Free-ranging elephants at close range - keep distance, stay in the vehicle, never between a matriarch and calves; elephants can charge. Malaria the main health risk. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:50Z","page_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00","source_country":"kenya","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Mandera, Wajir and Garissa counties","lvl":4,"note":"The Somalia border counties."},{"name":"Lamu County","lvl":4},{"name":"Tana River","lvl":4},{"name":"Kilifi north of Malindi","lvl":4},{"name":"The northern border areas","lvl":4},{"name":"Eastleigh, Nairobi","lvl":3},{"name":"Kibera, Nairobi","lvl":3}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"KE","source":"UK FCDO, Mar 2025","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry, clearest Kilimanjaro, wildlife at the marshes) + Jan-Feb (dry, clear mountain)","shoulder":"Nov + Mar (quieter, softer rates)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, quiet, cheapest; mountain often clouded)","booking_lead":"lodges + Kenya-circuit 4-9 mo for Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb (under-Kili luxury sells out); shoulder 2-4 mo; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Apr-May green-season value; combine Maasai Mara / Tsavo / Laikipia (rhino)","event_peaks":"Jun-Oct + Christmas/NY + Easter; N-Hemisphere summer","fire_date":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb clear-mountain safaris 6-9 mo out; green value by prior Nov-Dec; bundle Amboseli + Laikipia (rhino) to complete the Big Five"},"jewels":[{"name":"Elephants under Kilimanjaro (Super Tuskers)","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$400-2,000/pp/day","timing":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb; dawn","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the most iconic image in safari — great herds and giant-tusked bulls crossing the dust with the snow-capped 5,896-m peak behind","si":"safari","blurb":"the most iconic image in safari — great herds and giant-tusked bulls crossing the dust with the snow-capped 5,896-m peak behind","when":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb; dawn","commission":"safari DMC 10-16%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":16,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Observation Hill + the swamp game","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"within the safari","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"climb the park''s one hill for the panorama of the snowmelt swamps, then game-drive the marsh edges where elephant, buffalo","si":"safari","blurb":"climb the park''s one hill for the panorama of the snowmelt swamps, then game-drive the marsh edges where elephant, buffalo","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"safari DMC 10-16%","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":16,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Dawn hot-air balloon over Amboseli","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$400-500/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sunrise over the elephant plains with Kilimanjaro on the horizon, then a bush breakfast — the signature aerial view","si":"adventure","blurb":"sunrise over the elephant plains with Kilimanjaro on the horizon, then a bush breakfast — the signature aerial view","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"DMC/camp 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"The Amboseli Elephant Research Project","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the longest wild-elephant study on Earth — 3,500+ named individuals, matriarchal society; behind-the-scenes conservation-tourism visits with the Trust","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the longest wild-elephant study on Earth — 3,500+ named individuals, matriarchal society; behind-the-scenes conservation-tourism visits with the Trust","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"conservation/DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A luxury-lodge honeymoon under Kilimanjaro","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$700-2,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Kilimanjaro-view honeymoon lodge","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","si":"romance","blurb":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Maasai village visit","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-50/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maasai who share the Amboseli ecosystem — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","si":"culture","blurb":"the Maasai who share the Amboseli ecosystem — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"DMC/community","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Amboseli?","a":"Elephants and remoteness. Amboseli''s herds are large and free-ranging - keep a respectful distance, stay in the vehicle and follow your guide (elephants can charge if threatened). Malaria is the main health risk (prophylaxis + DEET), and the park is remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days) + travel-medical insurance.","source":"kws.go.ke","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Amboseli - for game and Kilimanjaro?","a":"Jun-Oct and Jan-Feb (dry) - wildlife concentrates at the marshes and the mountain is clearest; go on a game drive at first light, before the summit hides behind cloud by ~10am. The green season is lush and better value.","source":"safaribookings.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Will I actually see Kilimanjaro and Super Tuskers?","a":"Often, but not guaranteed - the peak is cloud-shy, so plan multiple dawn drives for the clear-mountain shot. Amboseli is also one of the last strongholds of giant-tusked bulls; a good guide and a couple of days maximise both.","source":"privatetourscapetown.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is there rhino at Amboseli?","a":"No - rhino were hunted to local extinction here in the 1970s, so Amboseli is a four-of-the-Big-Five park (elephant, lion, buffalo, leopard). For rhino, pair it with Ol Pejeta/Lewa in Laikipia.","source":"delfintours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Kenya?","a":"An eTA (Kenya replaced visas with the eTA in 2024 - apply at least 2 weeks ahead). Yellow fever is compulsory only if you arrive from a YF-risk country; CDC recommends the vaccine for most.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Amboseli Safari Guide: Elephants Under Kilimanjaro, Super Tuskers, Best Time & Fees","meta_description":"Plan an Amboseli safari - elephants under Kilimanjaro, some of the last Super Tuskers, the iconic mountain view (clearest at dawn Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb), four of the Big Five, the 1972 elephant-research legacy, 2026 fees and cost, with real safety, timing and evac intel.","slug":"amboseli-kenya","primary_keyword":"Amboseli safari","long_tail":["Amboseli elephants Kilimanjaro","Amboseli Super Tuskers","best time to visit Amboseli","Amboseli park fees 2026","Amboseli vs Maasai Mara","is Amboseli safe","Amboseli balloon safari"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Amboseli","Kilimanjaro","tembo","Wamaasai","Kilima cha theluji","safari ya puto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-31","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-31","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:50Z","source_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["exercise-increased-caution","crime","urban-unrest"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"safe licensed-operator safari. Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - primary safari not globaladv; balloon/Kilimanjaro-photography = globaladv; elephant-research legacy = deepdive; NO rhino here; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"elephants + Super Tuskers; 4 of Big Five (no rhino)"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"balloon + Kilimanjaro photography + Observation Hill"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Amboseli Elephant Research Project (1972)"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"Maasai"}],"ultra":[{"name":"ol Donyo Lodge (Great Plains, Chyulu Hills) - the apex Kili view","why_ultra":"starbeds + plunge-pool suites with Kilimanjaro across the plains, horse-riding + walking on a private wilderness","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-2,800+/night"},{"name":"A private Amboseli + elephant-research day + balloon","why_ultra":"exclusive-vehicle safari + a behind-the-scenes elephant-research visit + the dawn balloon","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Big-Five-completing week (Amboseli + Laikipia + Mara)","why_ultra":"elephants-and-Kili + rhino in Laikipia + the migration in the Mara, private-guided throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Amboseli National Park, Kenya"},"geo":{"lat":-2.65,"lng":37.26},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["laikipia-kenya","maasai-mara-kenya","samburu-kenya","tsavo-kenya"]}'::jsonb, 4),
  ('bwindi-impenetrable-uganda', '05A', 'Bwindi Impenetrable National Park', 'Uganda', 'Half the world''s mountain gorillas', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Uganda — Bwindi / SW gorilla country', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","deepdive","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect gorilla demand to Rwanda Volcanoes","The world''s premier gorilla forest (UNESCO 1994): ~459 mountain gorillas - nearly HALF the world''s - across ~25 habituated groups (9 for trekking) in an ancient Afromontane rainforest","Permit $800 (foreign non-resident; $600 low-season Apr/May/Nov), operator-only since 1 Mar 2026; the Uganda-ONLY 4-hour Gorilla Habituation Experience (Rushaga) $1,500 -> $1,800 on 1 Jan 2027 (all latent while held)","One of Earth''s most biodiverse forests: 200+ trees, 350+ birds (Albertine Rift endemics), 202 butterflies; the Batwa first people","Yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); malaria in all regions incl. Bwindi (prophylaxis); strenuous steep/muddy trek (sectors Buhoma easiest, Nkuringo hardest) - all latent while held","Live twin = volcanoes-np-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable). Trek rules when reopened: 7-10m distance, mandatory mask, max 1hr, max 8/group, armed ranger, min age 15, no trekking if ill"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kihihi/Kampala (all latent while held)","malaria":"present in all regions incl. Bwindi lowland forest - prophylaxis (latent while held)","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17 - the dominant, disqualifying hazard","activity_note":"HEALTH-SPINE DOMINANT: Ebola outbreak is the hazard. FCDO BASIS (gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda, read 2026-08-20): health screening on arrival and departure; Ugandan border with the DRC closed from 27 May per the National Task Force; the UK Returning Workers Scheme activated due to the outbreak. NOTE THE FCDO ADVISES AGAINST NO TRAVEL TO UGANDA - posture 1 - so any book-suppression here is OUR health judgement, not an advisory one, and is DAVID''S CALL - CONTENT-ONLY, Book suppressed, no waiver, redirect to Rwanda. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle. Gorilla-trek + malaria hazards secondary and moot while held. When reopened: trek rules 7-10m/mask/1hr/max8/armed ranger/no-trek-if-ill; YF mandatory; strenuous high-forest hike","booking_hold":false,"fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-08-20T14:48:47Z","page_updated":"2026-07-27T15:00:28+01:00","source_country":"uganda","quotes_note":"posture re-joined 2026-08-30 from handoff/fcdo-advisories/uganda.json, which was corrected 2026-08-23. The previous AREA-RESTRICTED was derived from prose about a NEIGHBOURING country.","posture_basis":"alert_status empty; quoted sentences name another country","posture_corrected":"2026-08-23 - was AREA-RESTRICTED, derived from prose about a neighbour"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"latent_peak":"Jun-Aug/Sep + Dec-Feb (drier, firmer trails; permits scarce) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Apr/May + Nov (rains, muddier; $600 low-season permit)","latent_booking_lead":"permits + lodges 3-6 mo - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; flip Bwindi to live the moment it drops below","redirect":"live gorilla demand -> volcanoes-np-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable,, ~2h from Kigali)"},"jewels":[{"name":"The mountain-gorilla trek","si_tag":"safari","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path ($800 permit latent)","timing":"HELD; latent Jun-Aug + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":null,"hook":"nearly half the world''s mountain gorillas in an ancient UNESCO forest — a one-hour habituated-family encounter on a $800 permit. STATUS: HELD","si":"safari","blurb":"nearly half the world''s mountain gorillas in an ancient UNESCO forest — a one-hour habituated-family encounter on a $800 permit. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD; latent Jun-Aug + Dec-Feb","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"evidenced","deepdive":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The 4-hour Gorilla Habituation Experience","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"ultra","price_band":"HELD ($1,500 -> $1,800 2027 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Uganda-only — four hours with a semi-habituated family and the researchers, in the Rushaga sector. STATUS: HELD","si":"adventure","blurb":"Uganda-only — four hours with a semi-habituated family and the researchers, in the Rushaga sector. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","source":"https://www.silverbackgorillatours.com/gorilla-habituation-experience-in-bwindi-uganda","accessed":"2026-08-01","source_carried":true,"source_basis":"carried from the dossier lane source; the proper noun ''Gorilla Habituation Experience'' from the jewel name appears in the URL. NOT a human read of the jewel."},{"name":"The biodiversity of an ancient forest","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"one of Earth''s most biodiverse Afromontane rainforests — 200+ trees, 350+ birds, 202 butterflies. STATUS: HELD","si":"deepdive","blurb":"one of Earth''s most biodiverse Afromontane rainforests — 200+ trees, 350+ birds, 202 butterflies. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Batwa cultural experience","si_tag":"culture","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the forest''s first people — a moving visit to Batwa communities on the forest edge, their music, hunting heritage and displacement story. STATUS: HELD","si":"culture","blurb":"the forest''s first people — a moving visit to Batwa communities on the forest edge, their music, hunting heritage and displacement story. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","deepdive":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A forest-lodge gorilla honeymoon (held)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"held","tier":"luxury","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Bwindi Lodge, Sanctuary Gorilla Forest Camp, Clouds Mountain Gorilla Lodge — fireside forest luxury after the trek","si":"ultra","blurb":"Bwindi Lodge, Sanctuary Gorilla Forest Camp, Clouds Mountain Gorilla Lodge — fireside forest luxury after the trek","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I trek gorillas instead, right now?","a":"Rwanda - Volcanoes National Park. **FCDO travel advice for Uganda:** the FCDO names no advisory against travel to Uganda. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda — page updated 2026-07-27.*","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Bwindi?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. For a firm 2026 trip, book Rwanda now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Bwindi offer when it reopens?","a":"The world''s premier gorilla forest - nearly half the planet''s mountain gorillas, the $800 permit (cheaper than Rwanda), the Uganda-only 4-hour Habituation Experience, exceptional biodiversity and the Batwa culture. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"whc.unesco.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When it reopens, how hard is the Bwindi trek and what are the rules?","a":"Moderate-to-strenuous - 1-6 hours through steep, muddy forest (sectors from easy Buhoma to hard Nkuringo); then max 1 hour, 7-10m distance, a mandatory face mask, max 8 per group, an armed ranger, and no trekking if ill (gorillas are highly susceptible to human disease).","source":"kabiza.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions incl. Bwindi); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_description":"What it is, why it''s held, and where to trek gorillas instead (Rwanda''s Volcanoes NP).","slug":"bwindi-impenetrable-uganda","primary_