:"culture","blurb":"the proud Samburu people — a manyatta visit, warriors'' dances and beadwork with a fair-trade, community-benefiting operator","when":"Jul-Sep  + Jan-Feb","commission":"DMC/community","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A river-lodge honeymoon (Saruni / Sasaab)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$600-1,600+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Samburu''s distinctive lodges — Saruni''s rock-set suites, Sasaab''s Moroccan-Swahili tents over the Ewaso Ng''iro — private, stylish and quiet; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"Samburu''s distinctive lodges — Saruni''s rock-set suites, Sasaab''s Moroccan-Swahili tents over the Ewaso Ng''iro — private, stylish and quiet; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Samburu river honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jul-Sep  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jul-Sep  + Jan-Feb","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Samburu?","a":"The northern-frontier context and remoteness. Stick to the licensed-operator reserve programme (fly-in recommended over long northern road transfers), follow your guide with dangerous game, and carry AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days) + travel-medical insurance - public EMS is limited in the north. Malaria prophylaxis is essential.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Samburu different from the Mara or Amboseli?","a":"The Special Five - Grevy''s zebra, reticulated giraffe, oryx, gerenuk and Somali ostrich you won''t see in the southern parks - plus top leopard in the riverine forest, elephants on the Ewaso Ng''iro, and far fewer vehicles. It''s the connoisseur''s Kenya.","source":"charmingsafariz.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Samburu?","a":"Jun-Sep and Jan-Feb (dry) - hot and dry, when wildlife concentrates on the river and game-viewing peaks (Jul-Sep is the sweet spot). The green rains bring lush scenery, birdlife and lower rates.","source":"samburureserve.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How many days do I need in Samburu?","a":"2-3 days is ideal to work the river circuits and find the Special Five plus leopard; it pairs naturally with Laikipia (rhino, an hour''s drive/short hop) or the Mara/Amboseli.","source":"africaunpacked.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Kenya?","a":"An eTA (Kenya replaced visas with the eTA in 2024 - apply at least 2 weeks ahead). Yellow fever is compulsory only if you arrive from a YF-risk country; CDC recommends the vaccine for most.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Samburu Safari Guide: The Special Five, Leopard, Best Time & Northern-Kenya Safety","meta_description":"Plan a Samburu safari - northern Kenya''s Special Five (Grevy''s zebra, reticulated giraffe, gerenuk, oryx, Somali ostrich), Kenya''s best leopard on the Ewaso Ng''iro, the Born Free legacy and far fewer vehicles - with the fly-in northern-Kenya safety picture, timing and cost.","slug":"samburu-kenya","primary_keyword":"Samburu safari","long_tail":["Samburu Special Five","Grevy''s zebra Samburu","Samburu leopard","best time to visit Samburu","Samburu vs Maasai Mara","is Samburu safe","Ewaso Ng''iro Samburu"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Samburu","Ewaso Ng''iro","punda milia wa Grevy","twiga","chui","Wasamburu","Elsa"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-31","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-31","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:50Z","source_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["exercise-increased-caution","crime"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Samburu is the SAFE MAINSTREAM safari zone but lies in northern Kenya where far-north border counties (Mandera, Wajir, Garissa; Route via fly-in; Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - primary safari not globaladv; camel safari + cultural walks = globaladv; Born Free/Elsa = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"Special Five, leopard, elephants"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"camel safari + cultural bush walks"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Born Free / Elsa the lioness"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"the Samburu people"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Saruni Samburu / Sasaab - the river''s apex stays","why_ultra":"dramatic rock-and-river suites, private guiding, camel safaris and the Special Five to yourselves","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$900-1,800+/night"},{"name":"A private Samburu fly-in + camel + culture week","why_ultra":"exclusive-vehicle Special-Five safari + a camel-back day + a Samburu cultural immersion, privately guided","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A northern-Kenya pairing (Samburu + Laikipia rhino)","why_ultra":"the Special Five + the rhino conservancies of Laikipia, private-guided fly-in throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Samburu National Reserve, Kenya"},"geo":{"lat":0.6,"lng":37.5333},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["amboseli-kenya","laikipia-kenya","maasai-mara-kenya","tsavo-kenya"]}'::jsonb, 16),
  ('tarangire-tanzania', '05A', 'Tarangire National Park', 'Tanzania', 'Tanzania''s biggest elephant herds under thousand-year-old baobabs', 'live', 'verified', 'elephant', 'Tanzania — Northern Safari Circuit', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Tanzania''s elephant capital - the country''s highest elephant concentration (300+ along the Tarangire River in the dry season) and the 2nd-highest wildlife density in Tanzania after the Serengeti","Signature giant baobabs (trunks up to ~30m around) across ~2,850 km2 (Tanzania''s 6th-largest park), ~118 km SW of Arusha - the natural first/last leg of the northern circuit","550+ bird species + dry-country specials (fringe-eared oryx, gerenuk, lesser kudu); lion/leopard/cheetah; four of the Big Five (no rhino)","disclose LGBTQ+ targeting consideration; travel with a licensed operator","Best Jun-Oct (dry - game on the river); green season Nov-May lush/birdy/quieter; permits walking safaris + night drives (uncommon on the northern circuit) + balloon","Sold via Tanzanian safari DMCs + camp consortia 10-20%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; TANAPA park fees + balloon fees are pass-through; TZS (~2,633/USD, USD is the safari currency); eVisa; AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999","hospital":"Remote/bush - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Arusha","malaria":"present (lower on the high northern circuit but real) - prophylaxis + DEET advised","yellow_fever":"not required direct from US/Europe; mandatory if transiting >12h through a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"disclose LGBTQ+ targeting - same-sex relations criminalized; travel with a licensed operator). On safari: elephant-dense driving (keep still/quiet, never between cow and calf), walking safari + night drive only with armed ranger, balloon at dawn (weight/weather limits). Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:17Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00","source_country":"tanzania","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry) - elephants + game concentrate on the Tarangire River; book 4-8 mo ahead","shoulder":"Nov + Feb-Mar (good rates, green flushes, fewer vehicles)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, birdy, cheapest; some camps close)","booking_lead":"premium camps 4-8 mo for Jun-Oct; green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"green-season birding (550+ species breeding); calving-season combo (Tarangire + Ndutu Jan-Feb)","event_peaks":"Jul-Sep + Christmas/NY; the dry-season elephant spectacle","fire_date":"Jun-Oct 6-9 mo out within the northern-circuit loop; green-season birding value by prior Nov-Jan; position as the 2-night elephant-and-baobab anchor, not a day-stop"},"jewels":[{"name":"The dry-season elephant spectacle","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct peak","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Tanzania''s largest elephant herds — hundreds gathering along the Tarangire River as the land dries — set against giant baobabs","si":"safari","blurb":"Tanzania''s largest elephant herds — hundreds gathering along the Tarangire River as the land dries — set against giant baobabs","when":"Jun-Oct peak","commission":"DMC/camp","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Dry-country specials + big cats","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"year-round; Jun-Oct best","draw_rank":2,"hook":"fringe-eared oryx, gerenuk and lesser kudu you won''t see on the plains","si":"safari","blurb":"fringe-eared oryx, gerenuk and lesser kudu you won''t see on the plains","when":"year-round; Jun-Oct best","commission":"DMC/camp","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Walking + night safari + balloon","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$70-600/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tarangire is one of few northern-circuit parks that permits walking safaris and night drives","si":"adventure","blurb":"Tarangire is one of few northern-circuit parks that permits walking safaris and night drives","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Baobab + elephant ecology and a 550-bird list","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the giant baobabs and the elephants that shape them, plus one of the northern circuit''s richest bird lists","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the giant baobabs and the elephants that shape them, plus one of the northern circuit''s richest bird lists","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/specialist","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Chem Chem / Swala honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$800-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Chem Chem''s design-forward suites between Tarangire and Manyara, or Sanctuary Swala''s tented camp under the acacias by a waterhole","si":"ultra","blurb":"Chem Chem''s design-forward suites between Tarangire and Manyara, or Sanctuary Swala''s tented camp under the acacias by a waterhole","when":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Tarangire honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Tarangire?","a":"Not the parks - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southern Mtwara Region (terrorism, far away) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). In Tarangire itself the risks are ordinary safari ones: stay in-vehicle near game, keep distance from elephants, malaria prophylaxis.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why go to Tarangire - is it worth a night?","a":"Emphatically - it has Tanzania''s biggest elephant herds and its second-densest game after the Serengeti, in a landscape of giant baobabs most of the circuit lacks; many travelers treat it as a day-stop, but a 2-night stay in the dry season is one of the northern circuit''s best-value highlights.","source":"owsl.co.tz","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Tarangire?","a":"The dry season, Jun-Oct, when the Tarangire River is the only water for miles and elephants, buffalo and predators concentrate along it; the green season (Nov-May) is lush, excellent for birding (550+ species) and much quieter.","source":"owsl.co.tz","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure (~2-10 business days). Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya - key for Kenya-Tanzania combos.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How does Tarangire fit a northern-circuit itinerary?","a":"Beautifully - it''s ~118 km SW of Arusha, so it''s the natural first or last park, paired with Lake Manyara, the Ngorongoro Crater and the Serengeti on a classic 5-8-day loop.","source":"resiliencesafaris.com","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tarangire National Park Guide: Elephants, Baobabs, Best Time & Safari Costs","meta_description":"Plan a Tarangire safari - Tanzania''s elephant capital and the northern circuit''s underrated gem: the largest elephant herds in the country, ancient baobabs, 550+ birds and game second only to the Serengeti - with the FCDO advisory, best time (Jun-Oct), walking safaris and where to stay.","slug":"tarangire-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Tarangire National Park safari","long_tail":["Tarangire elephants baobabs","Tarangire best time to visit","Tarangire walking safari","Tarangire vs Serengeti","is Tanzania safe safari","Tarangire birding"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Tarangire","tembo","mbuyu","simba","pori"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:17Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-terrorism-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator. Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game is safari (PRIMARY here - elephant capital), NOT globaladv; walking safari + night drive + balloon = globaladv; baobab/elephant ecology + 550 birds = deepdive; no rhino (four of Big Five); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"big-game - highest elephant concentration in Tanzania (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"walking safari + night drive + balloon"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Chem Chem / Swala"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"baobab/elephant ecology + 550 birds"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chem Chem / Little Chem Chem - the design-luxury apex","why_ultra":"a private-concession lodge between Tarangire and Manyara, walking safaris and a spa in elephant country","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,200-2,500+/night"},{"name":"A private baobab-country walking week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide safari: walking + night drives + the elephant spectacle + a balloon dawn, from an ultra camp","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The 2-night Tarangire anchor of a private northern-circuit safari","why_ultra":"Tarangire + Manyara + Ngorongoro + Serengeti, privately guided and flown, with Tarangire given the room it deserves","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Tarangire National Park, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-3.8333,"lng":36},"orbit":[{"id":"lake-manyara-tanzania","jewels":6,"si":["safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"]}],"orbit_country":["ngorongoro-crater-tanzania","nyerere-selous-tanzania","ruaha-tanzania","serengeti-tanzania"]}'::jsonb, 17),
  ('tsavo-kenya', '05A', 'Tsavo National Park (East + West)', 'Kenya', 'Kenya''s great red wilderness', 'live', 'verified', 'elephant', 'Kenya — Tsavo', '{"safari","ultra","romance","adventure","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Kenya''s largest + oldest park - Tsavo East + West ~22,000 km2 (Tsavo East 13,747 km2), ~4% of Kenya; the great red wilderness of famous terracotta ''red elephants'' (dust-bathed in iron-rich soil)","A full Big Five park (unlike Amboseli): black rhino at the Ngulia Rhino Sanctuary (Tsavo West) + the maneless Tsavo lions; Mzima Springs crystal pools with an underwater hippo/croc observation chamber; Lugard Falls (Galana River)","The legend of the Man-Eaters of Tsavo (1898 lions that halted the Kenya-Uganda railway); on the historic Nairobi-Mombasa route","The uncrowded, BETTER-VALUE big-park alternative to the Mara (whose fees rose + circuits crowd); entry $80/non-resident; road 4-5h / SGR railway / charter from Nairobi; a natural Nairobi<->coast stopover","YF NUANCE: CDC recommends the yellow-fever vaccine for Taita-Taveta County (Tsavo) - treat YF as recommended here; malaria prophylaxis advised","Sold via KATO-member Kenya safari DMCs 15-25% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; KWS fees non-commissionable; KES (~129/USD) + M-Pesa but safari quoted USD; eTA required; AMREF for the size/remoteness"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112 / 911; Kenya Red Cross ambulance 1199 (often more reliable nationwide); AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Vast/remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Voi/Mombasa/Nairobi","malaria":"prophylaxis advised (Tsavo qualifies, chloroquine-resistant); DEET at dusk","yellow_fever":"compulsory if arriving from a risk country - AND CDC recommends the vaccine for Taita-Taveta County (Tsavo)","activity_note":"Dangerous game at close range (lion, elephant, hippo + croc at Mzima) - stay in the vehicle, view Mzima from the boardwalk/chamber only. VASTNESS: ~22,000 km2 sparsely-roaded - breakdowns far from help, experienced operator + fuel/water + evac cover. YF recommended (Taita-Taveta). Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:50Z","page_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00","source_country":"kenya","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Mandera, Wajir and Garissa counties","lvl":4,"note":"The Somalia border counties."},{"name":"Lamu County","lvl":4},{"name":"Tana River","lvl":4},{"name":"Kilifi north of Malindi","lvl":4},{"name":"The northern border areas","lvl":4},{"name":"Eastleigh, Nairobi","lvl":3},{"name":"Kibera, Nairobi","lvl":3}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"KE","source":"UK FCDO, Mar 2025","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb (dry - bush thins, wildlife at water, red elephants + Mzima easiest)","shoulder":"Nov + Mar (quieter, softer rates)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, birdlife, quietest, cheapest)","booking_lead":"lodges + Kenya-circuit 2-5 mo (Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb; less crunch than the Mara); shoulder/green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"Apr-May green-season value + birding; position as the uncrowded cheaper big park + Nairobi<->coast stopover; combine Amboseli or Mombasa/Diani beach","event_peaks":"Jun-Oct + Christmas/NY + Easter; coast-combo demand with beach season","fire_date":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb 3-5 mo out; value-vs-the-Mara + green bi